    "bbox": [
      48.0,
      233.96,
      420.03,
      283.4
    ],
    "reading_order": 7,
    "text": "Recall, a number ‘s’ is called irrational if it cannot be written in the form \n,\np\nq\nwhere p and q are integers and q ¹ 0. Some examples of irrational numbers, with\nwhich you are already familiar, are :",
    "latex": null,
    "image_ref": null,
    "confidence": 1.0
  },
  {
    "document_id": "NCERT_X_MATH_JEMH101",
