    "bbox": [
      48.0,
      391.2,
      294.73,
      402.2
    ],
    "reading_order": 11,
    "text": "*Proof : Let the prime factorisation of a be as follows :",
    "latex": null,
    "image_ref": null,
    "confidence": 1.0
  },
  {
    "document_id": "NCERT_X_MATH_JEMH101",
    "page": 6,
    "block_id": "jemh101_p006_b12",
    "type": "formula",
    "bbox": [
      72.0,
      409.68,
      391.59,
      423.31
    ],
    "reading_order": 12,
    "text": "a = p1p2 . . . pn, where p1,p2, . . ., pn are primes, not necessarily distinct.",
    "latex": null,
    "image_ref": null,
    "confidence": 1.0
  },
  {
    "document_id": "NCERT_X_MATH_JEMH101",
    "page": 6,
    "block_id": "jemh101_p006_b13",
    "type": "formula",
    "bbox": [
      48.0,
      428.07,
      262.4,
      441.79
    ],
    "reading_order": 13,
    "text": "Therefore, a2 = (p1p2 . . . pn)( p1p2 . . . pn) = p2",
    "latex": null,
    "image_ref": null,
    "confidence": 1.0
  },
  {
    "document_id": "NCERT_X_MATH_JEMH101",
    "page": 6,
